A||||5||Adrift||Car Stereo Question||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||10-22-2001||10:41 AM||||Can a MOSFET45 (45Wx4-Channel High Power) provide enough power for 6x9 4 ways and 6 1/2" 2 ways?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||10-22-2001||10:45 AM||||Generally you need 10-20 watts per speaker to drive a 6X9. You should be fine with that amp. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||10-22-2001||10:50 AM||||Thats 45 watts max...probably 20watts RMS.  It will power them like Oreif said.  Sounds like you are using the head unit to power them...there is no subsitute for a real amp.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Adrift||10-22-2001||10:55 AM||||Yes I am powering it with a head unit (http://www.competitionsound.com/dehp77dh.html) - I'm not looking to win any contests here, just want to have a good system.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fieronv||10-22-2001||11:44 AM||||Yes your head unit will power the 6x9's and it will sound okay. If you want your speakers to sound much better a seperate amp is a better option. You need to get an amp that is rated the same as your speakers. We are not talking blowing out your windows loud just good quality sound. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||10-22-2001||11:47 AM||||I do'nt care if you buy a $4000 head unit, the amp inside that thing is crammed in, with no cooling, consider the size, the parts used.<P>ANY external amp, even a cheap one will do a better job.  Well probably not ANY amp but you get the picture, head unit power is dirty, to say the least.<P>Yes it will power them, but don't even think for a minute you are actually going to be getting 45W, if you do it will have so much distortion in it, your speakers will probably blow from that distortion.<P><BR>Justin.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
